  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder so far (0.5203 acc, config_004), outperforming pca_n2000 (0.4849, config_001), while image-only is very weak (0.2079). The multiprofile axis is entirely untested. Question: Does multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve over singleprofile using the same scvi_n200 encoder? This isolates the effect of multiprofile+aggregation (the only change from config_004) while holding the RNA encoder fixed. Why this is best: With 6 experiments remaining, establishing whether multiprofile helps at all is the highest-priority design question before investing in more complex multimodal or transformer-aggregation variants. If multiprofile+avgpool does not beat 0.5203, it would redirect budget toward encoder exploration (scgpt) or multimodal fusion; if it does, it justifies testing transformer aggregation and multimodal extensions next."
}

